Mike Price wrote: <I would just say that we are (part of) the inside.>

This is what I find objectionable about the Ontological Proof of the Universe as
a Closed System.  "Inside" directly implies walls, or boundaries, or limits.
"Inside" does not exist as a logical concept without its complement "outside."
Since there is no "outside" the universe, there is no "inside" of the universe.
Defining coordinates for relative objects is strictly a mathematical concept
within our consensual reality for our own purposes, it is not a part of
objective reality.  It does not reduce the universe down to a defined system
because there are no limits anywhere to differentiate the "system" from anything
else.  The best you can do to define to the universe is to call it the opposite
of nothing, but nothing (the Void) does not exist in objective reality, so you
really haven't said anything.

